Subject: Serve polymorphic property-read hits before the slow handler

What this does
  A named read whose primary cache entry misses now tail-calls a small
  handler that probes the site's other ways. A hit stores the value borrowed,
  as the primary hit does, and keeps feeding the promotion credit; when the
  credit says the way should move to the primary it takes the full slow path,
  which performs the swap. A miss goes to a copy of the slow handler that
  skips the ways it just probed and tries the global stub cache and the full
  lookup. `get_this_field` gets the same probe. The slow handler rewrites the
  opcode byte only when the quickened form changes.

Why we need it
  Only the primary way was tested inline; every hit on another way, and on a
  two-prototype entry, went through the noinline slow handler, which also
  duplicated and parked the value and stored into the instruction stream.
  Octane deltablue spends about 10% of its instructions there.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.


